data: {"text":"1. My client, M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd., is a registered private limited company incorporated under the Companies Act, 2"}

data: {"text":"013, having its registered office at [address to be filled], and is engaged in the business of construction and"}

data: {"text":" infrastructure development. My client is a reputed contractor with extensive"}

data: {"text":" experience in executing government projects and has maintained an unblemished record in completing projects within"}

data: {"text":" stipulated timelines while adhering to all technical specifications and quality standards.\n\n2. My client was awarded a contract for construction of culverts on NH-31 vide Work Order No."}

data: {"text":" BRCD/PAT/2024/118 dated 12.06.2024 for a total contract value of Rs. 2,75,00,000/- (Rupees Two Cr"}

data: {"text":"ores Seventy-Five Lakhs only). The said work order was issued by your"}

data: {"text":" office and contained detailed specifications, timelines, and terms and conditions for the execution"}

data: {"text":" of the project, which my client accepted and commenced work accordingly.\n\n3. My client diligently executed all the"}

data: {"text":" contracted work with utmost care and precision, ensuring compliance with all technical specifications, quality parameters"}

data: {"text":", and safety norms as stipulated in the contract. The entire work was completed well within the stip"}

data: {"text":"ulated time frame by 28.02.2026, demonstrating my client's commitment to timely delivery and professional"}

data: {"text":" excellence.\n\n4. Upon completion of the work on 28.02.2026, my client submitted the"}

data: {"text":" final running bills along with measurement books duly signed by the site engineer, as required under the terms of the contract. All necessary documentation,"}

data: {"text":" certificates, and compliance records were submitted in accordance with the prescribed procedures and formats"}

data: {"text":" specified in the work order.\n\n5. Despite the satisfactory completion of work and submission of all"}

data: {"text":" requisite documents, your office has failed to release the final payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- (Rupees Eighty-Seven Lakhs Fifty Thousand only"}

data: {"text":") which has been outstanding since 28.02.2026. My client has made repeated representations through letters dated 05.03.2026"}

data: {"text":", 22.03.2026, and 18.04.2026, requesting immediate release of the outstanding payment, but no positive"}

data: {"text":" response has been received from your end.\n\n6. The wrongful withholding of the legitimate dues of Rs. 87,50,000"}

data: {"text":"/- has caused severe financial hardship to my client, affecting its cash flow, ability"}

data: {"text":" to service other commitments, and overall business operations. This delay has also caused reputational damage and has"}

data: {"text":" adversely impacted my client's standing in the market and its capacity to undertake future projects.\n\n7. I am const"}

data: {"text":"rained to serve this legal notice upon you in terms of Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, "}

data: {"text":"1908, which mandates that no suit shall be instituted against the Government or"}

data: {"text":" a public officer in respect of any act purporting to be done in official capacity until the expiration of two months next"}

data: {"text":" after notice in writing has been delivered to or left at the office of such"}

data: {"text":" public officer.\n\n8. NOTICE is hereby given that unless the outstanding payment of Rs. 87,50,000"}

data: {"text":"/- along with applicable interest is released within a period of sixty (60) days from the receipt"}

data: {"text":" of this notice, my client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate legal proceedings against you and your office for recovery"}

data: {"text":" of the said amount along with interest, costs, and such other reliefs as may be deemed fit by the Hon'ble Court"}

data: {"text":", without any further reference to you."}

